  "released": "1971-11-11",
  "notes": "Original cover layout with smaller font (no \"RE\" on cover).\n\nSerifed \"I\" stamped in runouts denotes [l=RCA Records Pressing Plant, Indianapolis], pressing. Remainder of runouts are stamped, except \"TML,\" which is etched.\n\nBack liner variation, with \"Cris Speddin\" in track credits instead of \"Cris Spedding.\"\n\nIssued on orange \"dynaflex\" labels, pressed on Dynaflex vinyl.\nIssued with 12\" × 24\" fold-out poster.\nIssued in Dynaflex company inner sleeve.\n\nSome copies with promo stamp/sticker/markings exist.\n\nCatalog number as LSP-4515 on back liner, spine, labels, poster; 5/LSP 4515 in price code on back cover.\nRCA Victor on back liner, labels; RCA on spine.\n\nArtist on spine: Harry Nilsson\n\nRecorded at Trident Studios, London - June 1971\nTracks B5 and A3 recorded in RCA Studios, Hollywood\nAdditional recording at Island Studios, London\nRemixed at Air, Island, Trident Studios, London and RCA Studios, Hollywood\nA Very Special Thanks to Doug Sax\n\nA Nilsson House Production\n\nPublic Performance Clearance - BMI except \"Without You\" - ASCAP\n\nTMK(s) ® by RCA Corporation © 1971 RCA Records, New York, N.Y.\nMade in U.S.A. Printed in U.S.A.",
  "released_formatted": "11 Nov 1971",
